dxc5 Qc7 9. Nf3 Nd7 10. Be3 b6 11. Be2 Nf5 12. O-O Nxe3 13. fxe3 Nxe5 14. Qg5
Nd7 15. c6 f6 $2 16. Nd4 Ne5 17. Qg3 (17. Rxf6+ $1 gxf6 18. Qxf6+ Kg8 19. Rf1
$18) 17... Qd6 $2 18. Nb5 {Source: British Championship, Aberystwyth 1961,
compiled by Eric Fisher. Contributed by Andy Ansel, 19 May 2023 & partial
moves, Illustrated London News, 2 September 1961. BH Wood doesn't give the
names of the players! But he does say this is from the first round of the
British Championship, and there is sufficient evidence from CHESS, 26 August
1961, p364 to indicate that this was Ellison-Lloyd (Opening moves as given,
then "Lloyd scattered Ellison's pawns like chaff but at a fatal cost in
development. The finish was neat and drastic.")} 1-0

