1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. Nc3 b5 6. Bd3 Bc5 7. Nb3 Ba7 8. O-O
Nc6 9. Qe2 Qh4 10. a4 b4 11. Nd5 exd5 12. exd5+ Nce7 13. d6 Bb7 14. g3 $2 Qf6
$2 (14... Qh3 $1 15. Be4 Qe6 $1 $19) 15. Bf4 Qe6 16. Rfe1 Nf6 17. Na5 Bd5 18.
dxe7 (18. Qd2 $18) 18... Ng4 19. Nc4 Bc5 20. Nd6+ Bxd6 21. Qxe6 fxe6 22. Bxd6
a5 23. Rac1 Nf6 24. c3 bxc3 25. Rxc3 Ng8 26. f4 Nxe7 27. f5 Nc6 28. Bb5 Rc8 29.
Ba6 Rd8 30. Bb7 Kf7 31. Bc7 Rde8 32. fxe6+ Rxe6 33. Rxe6 $2 (33. Rd1 $1) 33...
Kxe6 34. Rc5 $2 Rf8 35. Bxc6 Bxc6 36. Re5+ Kf6 37. Rxa5 Re8 38. Kf2 $2 (38. b4
$16) 38... Re4 {"My game with Franklin was also full of excitement and missed
chances. After making a temporary piece sacrifice to keep Black's King in
the centre I made an error which should have prevented me from recovering it.
Fortunately, Franklin did not see it either, and the game went on with White
holding the advantage as before. This I succeeded in converting into an extra
pawn with the better ending, but in the time rush and with Franklin resisting
tenaciously I failed to obtain any more out of it. A draw was a fair result." 
(PH Clarke, BCM, October 1961, p275. Source: British Championship, Aberystwyth
1961, compiled by Eric Fisher. Contributed by Andy Ansel, 19 May 2023.} 1/2-1/2

